# Container CI/CD implementation pattern

- Make CI/CD changes on a dedicated `feat/` branch and begin with an implementation plan.
- Use separate lint, build, scan, and publish jobs; use matrices for independent image builds and pushes.
- Keep publish credentials isolated to the final trusted publish job. Prefer GitHub OIDC and short-lived cloud credentials over stored secrets.
- Pull requests must validate without cloud authentication or publishing. Keep vulnerability gates fail-closed unless an explicitly documented manual override is required.
- Pin third-party actions to exact release versions and give workflow jobs the minimum permissions needed.
